WEBVTT

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.430
--Gambee 06 to Platform #9!
--Put out the fire! Quickly!

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:10.400
The unit won't last much longer!
Pull the pilot out, quick!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.170
Malfunction with the cockpit release!

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.000
Opening with an EM Cutter!

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.140
Medic!

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.050
--Hurry up!
--R-right!

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.890
The pilot appears to have
head injuries! H-her pulse is...

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.060
Her pulse is weak!
Emergency procedures are required!

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.650
Performing manual seatbelt release!

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.660
U-uhh... Where was it again?

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.730
The switch! The switch!
Where's the switch?!

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.000
W-where is it?! Where?!

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.880
What do I do?! Tell me!
What do I do? What do I do?!

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.540
Eh? What?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.010
T-time... The time!

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.180
That's enough, Cadet Becky Balboa!

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.820
Cadet Sara Cruz is dead.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.020
Eh?!

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.680
O-oh no!

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.190
I killed someone again!

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.820
Sub-Light Speed Nightmare

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.480
I did it again...

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.120
It's only an exercise.
Don't take it so hard.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.820
H-having you say that is a relief...

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.260
Oh, that reminds me. Earlier, you...

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.820
Oh, yeah.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.390
I tried to say that the switch was
in the panel to your lower right.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.850
Hey, you! Quit freaking out
and drag the body out already!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.940
Come on, Engineering Division!
Be better prepared!

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.740
Come on! Next team!
Get moving! Are you even ready?!

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.480
You put out fires too slow!
You're too slow opening the cockpit!

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.380
You're gonna kill the Gambee pilots!

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.780
I'm sorry... I'm always so stupid...

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:06.860
Oh, my. Cadet Cruz has passed away.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.790
If only she really would die.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.870
This concludes this
tri-division joint exercise,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.200
but as today's chief instructor,
I would like to say one thing.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.010
You're deplorable!

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:29.080
It's only been four days
since we took the Libertad,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.080
Basion Tactical Training
School's mother ship,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.320
out for sub-light speed exercises.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.690
But one month has already
passed for Basion!

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.690
Those cadets who weren't able
to participate in these exercises

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.590
have probably greatly improved by now!

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.130
Participation in the sub-light
exercises is not a goal!

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:49.430
Lose focus one bit and you'll be
left behind in the blink of an eye!

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.270
In particular, I've seen many
Gambee pilots who see this as a game!

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.900
It is truly mortifying!

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.940
Like a certain corpse who acted foolishly?

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.500
He's talking about you, Isabella!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.940
That is all! Dismissed!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.280
That's an interesting look, Sara Cruz!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.070
Are those lowlifes hassling you again?

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.300
Did they toss out your
clothes or something?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.540
Okay!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.600
In that case, you leave me no choice!
You can have my spare-

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.780
You can have Jessie's clothes!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.080
Eh?! Mine?!

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.920
Oh... Right here?

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.720
No, thanks.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.520
Eh? But...

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.930
She's as unpleasant a person as ever.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:28.660
Then why do you care so much about her?
Even the other day, you...

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.440
There's something about her that's
a lot like me. I'm curious.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.240
Like you? Are you sure?

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.010
What's the occasion?
Why are you stripping out here?

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.380
Hold on, Dickon!
What are you doing?!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.880
Was she that Gambee pilot?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.810
You were watching, Carris?

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.290
It's not that often when it's
the Queen who gets the cold shoulder!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.020
Yeah, that was her.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.130
Despite being a transfer student,
she underwent grueling self-training

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.100
and eventually got permission to join
the sub-light speed exercises!

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.470
She's got guts, that Sara Cruz!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.900
Guts, huh?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.300
Quit it!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:18.280
Hey, you! What do you think you're
doing, coming in here so filthy?!

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.150
This isn't only your room, you know!

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.620
She must be crazy.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.820
I can't remember...
did she play a corpse?

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.990
No point trying to talk to a corpse.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:29.690
Then she should go sleep
in her grave instead.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:32.430
No, I know! She must be a zombie!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.720
Yuck!

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.010
Melchi! That's not what we agreed to!
What're you changing?!

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.780
Shut up, Carmichael!
It's cooler this way!

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.350
Is not!

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.480
What?!

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.020
--Fix it! This instant!
--Nope!

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.280
What?!

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.190
Hey! Don't run away!

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:01.960
--Where's Emily?
--Eh? The same place as always.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.130
--"Emily"?
--That doll with the Mimic inside!

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:09.630
Why don't you learn her name already?
She comes here everyday!

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.870
I don't care what names
other people give her!

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.130
I was the one who originally
created her, after all!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.810
Hi, Emily. I have
a present for you today.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:26.010
I tried making this.
What do you think?

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.380
Hmm, I dunno. It doesn't
really match those clothes.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.230
That wasn't a very
nice way of putting it.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:42.060
If your clothes don't match it,
then I'll make you some new ones.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.400
Hmm, maybe have this like so?

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:51.010
This is no good, either! Why can't
it support a load of this level?!

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.010
'Cause you have it at crazy settings
to increase its reaction time...

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.510
But that's its best feature!
I can't change that!

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:01.150
Then why not test it with her?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:06.990
She's not a standard Mimic,
so who knows, it could work better!

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:12.330
Forget it. I'd have to reconfigure
the whole cockpit for that.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.560
But what to do?

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.430
We're not going to get
anywhere unless it starts up...

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:21.940
It'll be so awesome if it works!
It'll even turn the tide of the war!

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.430
Key word being "if..."

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.280
We will now conduct the
sub-light speed combat exercise.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.880
Though, as Gambees are far
less maneuverable than Strains,

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:37.590
they will be used
as gun batteries this time.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:42.460
But don't sub-light speed
battles hardly ever happen?

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.260
But not "never."

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.860
It's for that very reason
that we conduct this training

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.870
during sub-light speed exercises.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.870
Any other questions?

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.960
Then all hands, to your stations!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.320
Control. Gambee 606 won't activate.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.820
What? You can just watch, then! Come down!

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.370
Whatever you do, do not leave the ship!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:29.670
The instant you do, you'll be swept away,
left to drift through space!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.170
And of course, never attack forward!

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:36.480
At sub-light speed, attacks
will always fall backwards!

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:41.810
Attack forward, and you'll end up
with the full brunt of it yourself!

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.690
TUMORs?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.460
The Mobile Troops Division is conducting
sub-light combat training.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.290
Maybe they're their targets?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.660
But, the sheer number of them...

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:57.190
Encountering the enemy during
sub-light speed travel is unheard of.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.460
--Double-check it.
--Yes, sir...

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:06.710
This is a training school's exercise voyage.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.200
We're not even worth attacking.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.050
Move aside a second!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:17.450
No... It can't be!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.960
Captain! It's the enemy!
They have our front side!

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.980
What?!

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.850
Escort Ship #1 has been downed!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.790
All ships, move to Combat Deployment #1!

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.990
Emergency acceleration!
Take the enemy's front!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.990
Commencing Mercurion reaction
activation! Increasing output!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.400
Captain! Wouldn't it be
better to shake them off

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.130
by decelerating suddenly
or altering our course?

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.700
Don't be foolish!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:10.110
We'd crush the ship flat if we
jumped out of sub-light speed!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:14.640
Same goes for changing course!
What do they teach you in school?!

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.610
1% acceleration! We're moving ahead!

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:18.850
Prepare to attack!

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.370
Don't shoot forward, now!
Only sideways or backwards!

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.890
An enemy attack?!

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.220
The first escort ship has
already been shot down.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.390
They will likely engage
the second escort ship momentarily.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:35.630
Go to the bridge and take command
of the Mobile Troops Division.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.830
Yes, sir!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.830
Hear that, fledglings?

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.840
Our generous Deague guests
are going to give you

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.970
some real-life combat experience.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.240
--Attack carefully!
--Roger!

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.540
Alright. You'll support
the Gambees from here.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.880
Yes, sir!

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.080
Instructor! What should I do?!

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:59.420
We can't prepare a unit for
you now! Just stay here!

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.190
All Strains, launch!

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:06.490
Don't let the enemy get any closer!

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.800
The way the first ship went down...

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.400
Simple TUMORs slamming into
it wouldn't have caused that.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.060
It couldn't be...

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.070
Displaying video of the enemy!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.010
T-this is...

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:24.600
A Gloire Type! Ralph Werec's Strain?!

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.590
The second ship... has been shot down!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.800
W-what? This can't be...

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.530
The enemy is about to cross our
ship's secondary defense line!

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.240
Gloire Type Strain confirmed!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.670
It's definitely the squad
that attacked Grabera!

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:55.370
Ralph Werec... Why would you
attack a training fleet like us?!

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:00.580
All cadets are ordered to move out!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:05.320
Launch all Strains! Gambee squads,
protect the ship from TUMORs!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.590
All hands, scramble! This is not a drill!

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:12.220
I repeat, this is not a drill!

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.730
We're up against a Strain.
A Gloire Type and TUMORs.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.400
They've already destroyed two
escort ships and are headed for us.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:27.980
Everyone, think back to yesterday's
sub-light combat training!

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.750
Don't shoot forward.
Right, Instructor Dufarge?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.880
Correct!

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.650
And one other thing:

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:36.580
two-way communication isn't
possible at sub-light speed.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.950
Each unit will be fighting
on its own accord.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.520
Do not act recklessly!

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.760
We're fighting our first battle
in this situation.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.060
It doesn't get any more
reckless than that!

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.220
All Strains have launched!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:14.160
Don't get lured out! Gambees won't
be able to fight outside the ship!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.960
You'll all go to the outer trenches

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.790
and shoot off TUMORs
that've attached to the ship!

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.060
What the hell?!

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:26.230
Our first fight is a sub-light speed
battle?! You gotta be kidding me!

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:28.700
Unless you want to visit
the afterlife, get moving!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.070
--You idiot! Don't push!
--What're you doing?!

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:33.110
You're in the damn way!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:36.640
The Reasoners are gonna get all
the glory if we just sit around!

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.380
What are you doing?!
Platoon 6-0 has Route 115!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:43.820
Platoon 81, Platoon 54!
Head to the upper pathway from there!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.390
I'm going to give you a detour route!
Please follow it!

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.860
Opening lower starboard pathway! Hurry!

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.830
Hey, did you hear?!
The enemy's got a Strain with them!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:58.370
Whoa, no way! Are you saying
we're up against the Ralph Werec?!

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.600
You can't be serious!

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:02.930
My brother... is here?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:16.950
My brother... is right outside...

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.850
He's right out there...

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:23.260
But I can't even go into space...

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:27.250
Why am I here? Why?!

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:38.370
You fool! You're a goner
if you fight like that!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.770
Should've listened!

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:51.450
I can't bother with these things!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.980
I have to find him... Ralph Werec!

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:02.800
Our first group of guests has arrived!
Give them a warm welcome!

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:06.230
Don't be hasty! Just wait
until they're at your side!

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:10.440
Yes! I could take care of these all myself!

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:12.100
Isabella! Above you!

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:17.110
W-wait! No!

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:19.550
No! No! Help!

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:20.480
Isabella!

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.010
No!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:46.140
The ship's rate of acceleration
is falling! What's happening?!

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:49.380
The number of Strains lost has passed 30%!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.550
20% of the Gambees have been lost!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:57.280
How can this be happening?
They haven't even graduated yet...

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.570
Dammit! Where is everyone?!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.840
You're alright, Carris?!

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:18.970
Dickon! You see anyone else?!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:22.780
Ermy, Martha, and Lavinia are putting
up a fight on the right wing!

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:25.810
What about Jessie and the Queen?!

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:31.420
I'm fine! But Lottie heard
Ralph Werec is with the enemy and-

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.450
Where are you, Ralph Werec?!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.560
This looks kind of bad, huh?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.960
It's a real shock that we'd be
attacked in a place like this...

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.000
Why would they attack a ship like this?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.460
Honestly, what could the Deague be thinking?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.370
That explosion!

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.870
I found him! It's him!

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.340
I won't let him have his way anymore!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.110
You need something?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.520
We're busy having a pity party.

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.720
If it's unimportant, save it for later...

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:43.390
Wait, we'll be dead later, so you
wouldn't get to say anything...

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:47.660
This Strain is fully complete,
right? I'm getting in it!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:48.800
Huh?!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.800
But you're a Gambee pilot!

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:55.240
Not to mention people who don't
have Mimics can't pilot Strains!

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:58.640
But I do have a Mimic! Emily!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:01.510
Come on, now.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:05.810
Everyone knows you can't pilot
a Strain with someone else's Mimic.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.320
Honestly, now!

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.180
Go ahead.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.690
Let's give it a try!

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:15.190
I did just finish reconfiguring
the cockpit so that doll can use it!

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.890
It'll at least be a good
start-up test, right?

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.800
Let's go, Emily...

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.920
What a bummer...

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.290
This ship is done for.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:55.930
Unless a miracle somehow happens
and that Strain starts up...

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.530
Do you think it'll start?

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.270
Yeah, right.

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:03.700
I hope there'll be a miracle...

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.140
You can't pilot a Strain
with someone else's Mimic.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.250
I know that, but...

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:15.980
I'm not sure why, but it felt
like this girl called for me...

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:21.590
Yeah... That's it.
You called for me, right?

